# . EasyHybrid extension of pDynamo3 dyff-1.0 (2026-10-08): "dyff-1.0-eh".
#   Identical to dyff-1.0 except for the ADDITIONS marked "EasyHybrid" below; every atom typed
#   by dyff-1.0 keeps its type. Validation: DYFF_validation/report/new_types_report.html.
#     P:Res  aromatic P (phosphinines). Bond radius from the UFF bond rule (order 1.5, Pauling
#            bond-order and O'Keeffe-Brese electronegativity terms) solved for C-P = 1.733 A
#            (phosphabenzene; GFN2-xTB 1.734) -> 1.103.
#     Se:Res aromatic Se (selenophenes, selenazoles). Same rule for C-Se = 1.855 A (selenophene,
#            CCCBDB experimental, Hellwege 1976) -> 1.236.
#     Angles: these two-connected resonant atoms get the UFF GENERAL angle form (minimum at the
#            natural angle; dyff_edits.BENT_RESONANT_TYPES) instead of the trigonal 120-deg form
#            dyff-1.0 gives every Res atom. Their "Bond Angle" is an EFFECTIVE natural angle,
#            calibrated so that the DYFF-optimized parent ring reproduces the reference:
#              Se:Res 109.6 -> selenophene C-Se-C 87.77 deg (CCCBDB experimental)
#              P:Res   91.8 -> phosphabenzene C-P-C 99.9 deg (GFN2-xTB; no verified experimental value)
#            (it balances the stiff trigonal angles of the ring carbons, hence not the observed angle).
#     Charge, electronegativity and torsion U from the element (P, Se); torsion V = 0 (Res).
#     Transition metals (2026-10-13): geometry perceived from coordinates (pdynamo.metal_geometry), 175 new
#            types from tmQM; metal Bond Radius of every metal type calibrated on tmQM with CM5 (DYFF_validation
#            scripts/tmqm_calibrate.py, results/tmqm_calibration.json; the dyff-1.0 UFF metal radii included).
#
# . Atom types copied from UFF and put into DYFF-1.0 format.
